# Generated from: specs/349-namespace-controller-workers-across-retained-smoke-clones/requirements.md
Feature: Namespace controller workers across retained smoke clones
  The execute controller previously derived Herdr worker names
  only from issue and step, so a retained smoke clone's s<N>-start
  collided with a later clone for the same issue. This was fixed by
  namespacing worker names with a persisted per-run workerNamespace.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Fresh clone ignores another root's leftover issue worker
    Given two project roots share one Herdr agent inventory
    And root A has a live worker for issue 39 from a different run
    When root B starts execute for issue 39 with a new checkpoint
    Then B does not stop with retained_worker_mismatch because of A's worker
    And B does not close, prompt, or reuse A's pane
    And B starts a worker named s{ns}-39-start for B's persisted namespace

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Same-run restart keeps namespaced standard rem review and deliver workers
    Given a checkpoint records runId and workerNamespace
    When execute resumes in that project root and continues through review remediation and delivery
    Then worker names stay s{ns}-{issue}-{step} and r{ns}-{issue}-{step} from that namespace
    And retained reuse still requires matching ownership fields

  # --- Edge Case ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Legacy checkpoint does not claim a foreign worker
    Given a valid schemaVersion 1 checkpoint with no workerNamespace field
    When execute discovers a live s{issue}-* agent owned by another root or a malformed workerNamespace
    Then a missing field keeps legacy s{issue}-{step} names for this run only
    And a foreign agent is not prompted closed or recorded as this run's worker
    And a malformed workerNamespace stops with invalid_worker_namespace and starts no worker
